er_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Jacobs Solutions Inc. engages in the infrastructure and advanced facilities, and consulting businesses in the United States, Europe, Canada, India, Asia, Australia, New Zealand, the Middle East, and Africa. The company provides consulting, planning, architecture, design, engineering, and infrastructure delivery services including project, program, and construction management and long-term operation of facilities. It offers consulting services for consumer and manufacturing, defense and security, energy and utilities, financial services, government, health and life sciences, and transport sectors. Jacobs Solutions Inc. was founded in 1947 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert V. Pragada | CEO & Chair of the Board | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 47K people. Revenue per employee of $334K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $11K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Jacobs Solutions Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $17.0B market cap on $15.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 21% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $529M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.63\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 5.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 46% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.45922492241772944},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2078547.58},{"text":"Significant goodwill (40% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Is Driving Jacobs (NYSE:J) Latest Infrastructure Expansion?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/what-is-driving-jacobs-nysej-latest-infrastructure-expansion","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795718220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Jacobs (J) Q4 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/jacobs-j-q4-2026-earnings-153110000.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795534759.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Did Washington Airports Select Jacobs (NYSE:J) for Modernisation?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/why-did-washington-airports-select-jacobs-nysej-for-modernisation","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795526220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Jacobs Solutions (J) Said on Its Q4 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/jacobs-solutions-j-said-q4-001237322.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795479157.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Jacobs Solutions: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/jacobs-solutions-3-key-takeaways-061818631.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795587498.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Jacobs Solutions Analysts Boost Their Forecasts Following Upbeat Q4 Earnin